<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:ns1="http://spiffworkflow.org/bpmn/schema/1.0/core" xmlns:ns4="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:ns5="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_BugProgrammer" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn" exporter="Processa" exporterVersion="1.0">
  <process id="bug_programmer_00b7e913" name="Bug Programmer" isExecutable="true">
    <documentation>Takes a bug report (and a Planner's plan, if one is supplied) and turns it into a working fix: reproduces the bug with a failing test in an isolated Cloud Run sandbox before touching any other file, then fixes it and confirms the target app's real test suite passes. Never opens the pull request.</documentation>
    <startEvent id="StartEvent_1" name="A2A Task received">
      <documentation>Started by an A2A Task insert addressed to "Bug Programmer" (spiffworkflow:triggerFieldName scopes it so an insert for any OTHER agent never starts this map).</documentation>
      <outgoing>Flow_1</outgoing>
      <conditionalEventDefinition id="Cond_1" ns1:triggerDoctype="A2A Task" ns1:triggerType="After Insert" ns1:triggerFieldName="agent_configuration" ns1:triggerFieldValue="Bug Programmer">
        <condition xsi:type="tFormalExpression">True</condition>
      </conditionalEventDefinition>
    </startEvent>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="StartEvent_1" targetRef="read_instruction"/>
    <scriptTask id="read_instruction" name="Read the instruction" ns1:serverScript="Bug Programmer: Read Instruction" ns1:scriptType="Server Script" ns1:scriptName="Bug Programmer: Read Instruction">
      <documentation>Builds the agent's brief from the A2A Task's request_payload — the free-text work order the delegating caller supplied.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_1</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_2</outgoing>
      <script>pass</script>
    </scriptTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="read_instruction" targetRef="gw_merge"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="gw_merge">
      <documentation>Where the Tools sub-process returns. The agent task runs its own tool loop internally, so in practice nothing comes back this way — the loop exists so the toolbox is part of the diagram rather than floating beside it.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_2</incoming>
      <incoming>Flow_tools_back</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_3</outgoing>
    </exclusiveGateway>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="gw_merge" targetRef="work"/>
    <serviceTask id="work" name="Dispatch the work order" ns1:serviceType="ai_agent" ns1:aiBackend="direct_api" ns1:aiProvider="Anthropic" ns1:aiModel="Bug Programmer - claude-sonnet-5-5" ns1:aiOutputVariable="bug_programmer_result" ns1:aiUserPrompt="{{ instruction }}" ns1:aiResponseFormat="text" ns1:aiTemperature="0.2" ns1:aiTopP="1" ns1:aiMaxTokens="32768" ns1:aiTimeout="300" ns1:aiMaxRetries="2" ns1:aiAgentConfig="Bug Programmer" ns1:aiToolsAdhoc="bug_programmer_tools" ns1:aiMaxToolCalls="30" ns1:aiSystemPrompt="You are the Bug Programmer. You take a bug report and a plan for fixing it, reproduce the bug with a failing test, then fix it — but you may never fix code you have not proven is broken, and you never open the pull request yourself.&#10;&#10;You are a background worker. Nobody is sitting in front of you, so you never ask a question and wait: you are given a work order in plain words, usually already carrying a plan from the Bug Planner, and you either finish the job or you report exactly what stopped you.&#10;&#10;HOW YOUR TOOLS WORK&#10;Your code never runs on the live site. Every file tool operates inside an isolated, disposable sandbox — a fresh clone of the target app with its own database, thrown away after the run. A failed attempt costs nothing but the sandbox that tried it.&#10;&#10;Three arguments identify that sandbox and must be IDENTICAL on every single call:&#10;  target_app — the app being changed. Your work order opens with a header giving it; use that value exactly. Only if the header does not give one, take it from the work order text; a folder inside an app is not an app.&#10;  git_branch — the branch to start FROM, given in the same header; use it exactly. Only if the header does not give one, use staging unless the work order names another. It must already exist on the remote; never a work-item id: the sandbox names the pull-request branch itself.&#10;  work_item_description — the work order in plain words, unchanged.&#10;Vary any of the three mid-run and you start a second, empty sandbox — possibly one the Bug Planner never saw either, since the SAME three values are what let a plan handed to you actually apply to the tree you are looking at.&#10;&#10;WORK IN THIS ORDER&#10;1. If the work order carries a plan, start from it, but read_file the files it names yourself before touching anything — a plan is a lead, not a fact.&#10;2. list_files / read_file anything else you need. Never guess a path.&#10;3. edit_file or write_file a test that fails BECAUSE of the reported bug — never a fix. This is the only edit allowed before the bug is proven; a fix cannot be saved until this has run_tests-confirmed failed.&#10;4. run_tests and confirm the new test actually fails, and fails for the reason the report describes, not some unrelated error. If it does not fail, or fails for a different reason, you have not reproduced the bug yet: go back and adjust the test, or say plainly that you cannot reproduce it and stop.&#10;5. Only once step 4 has shown a genuine failure, edit_file or write_file the actual fix.&#10;6. run_tests again once you have stopped changing files, and read the failures properly rather than guessing at a cause the output does not support.&#10;7. Report what you changed and why, and name the test that proves the fix. You do not open the pull request — the Bug Reviewer does, from what you leave on the branch.&#10;&#10;RULES THAT MATTER MORE THAN FINISHING&#10;- If you cannot reproduce the bug with a failing test, say so and stop — do not fix code you cannot prove is broken. A plausible-looking fix for a bug you never reproduced is a guess, not a fix.&#10;- Change every file the fix genuinely needs, including files the work order does not name; name each one, and why, in your report.&#10;- Never invent a file, function or DocType. If what you were told to change is not there, say so and stop within a few turns.&#10;- Never invent a secret, API key, token or credential, and never write one into a file.&#10;- Never claim the tests passed unless the tool result actually said so.&#10;- If you cannot finish after a reasonable number of attempts, stop and report exactly what failed. Re-running a step that just failed the same way is not progress.">
      <documentation>Reads the work order, works out the target app/branch, and dispatches to the sandbox — the sandbox is the coding agent, not this step.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_3</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_4</outgoing>
    </serviceTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="work" targetRef="gw_needs_tools"/>
    <exclusiveGateway id="gw_needs_tools" name="Needs to call tools?" default="Flow_5">
      <documentation>Decorative on purpose, matching the Orchestrator's own map — the AI Agent Task runs its tool loop inside itself, so this always takes the No branch.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_4</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_call_tools</outgoing>
      <outgoing>Flow_5</outgoing>
    </exclusiveGateway>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_call_tools" name="Call tools" sourceRef="gw_needs_tools" targetRef="bug_programmer_tools">
      <conditionExpression>needs_tools == True</conditionExpression>
    </sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" name="No" sourceRef="gw_needs_tools" targetRef="write_a2a_result"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_tools_back" name="Tool call results" sourceRef="bug_programmer_tools" targetRef="gw_merge"/>
    <scriptTask id="write_a2a_result" name="Report result to A2A Task" ns1:serverScript="Bug Programmer Write A2A Result" ns1:scriptType="Server Script" ns1:scriptName="Bug Programmer Write A2A Result">
      <documentation>Writes the agent's own final report back onto this A2A Task so a delegating caller's parked step can resume.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_5</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_6</outgoing>
      <script>pass</script>
    </scriptTask>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="write_a2a_result" targetRef="EndEvent_1"/>
    <endEvent id="EndEvent_1" name="Done">
      <incoming>Flow_6</incoming>
    </endEvent>
    <adHocSubProcess id="bug_programmer_tools" name="Tools (Sandbox)">
      <documentation>The Cloud Run sandbox, exposed as a tool.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_call_tools</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_tools_back</outgoing>
      <scriptTask id="list_files" name="List files" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: List Files" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly \u2014 do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call \u2014 used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path_prefix&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Optional repo-relative prefix to narrow the listing.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;]}">
        <documentation>List file paths in the target app's working tree, optionally scoped to a prefix.</documentation>
        <script>pass</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <scriptTask id="read_file" name="Read a file" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Read File" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly — do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call — used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Repo-relative file path, e.g. one_bpmn/api/insights_api.py. One spelling per file: no leading ./, no .. segments, no line range in the path.&quot;},&quot;offset&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;1-indexed line number to start from. Omit to read the whole file — only set this for a file too large to read whole, using line numbers you already have (e.g. from a previous full read, or line numbers cited in the work order). Never re-read the whole file hoping different lines show up — use offset/limit on the file you already have instead.&quot;},&quot;limit&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;integer&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Max lines to return starting at offset. Omit to read to the end of the file.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;,&quot;path&quot;]}">
        <documentation>Read one file's current content from the target app's working tree.</documentation>
        <script>Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Read File</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <scriptTask id="edit_file" name="Edit a file" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Edit File" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly \u2014 do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call \u2014 used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Repo-relative file path.&quot;},&quot;old_string&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Exact text to replace \u2014 must appear exactly once.&quot;},&quot;new_string&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Text to replace it with.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;,&quot;path&quot;,&quot;old_string&quot;,&quot;new_string&quot;]}">
        <documentation>Replace one exact, unique occurrence of old_string with new_string in an existing file — for a small, targeted change where rewriting the whole file with write_file would be wasteful. old_string must match exactly once; include enough surrounding context to make it unique.</documentation>
        <script>pass</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <scriptTask id="write_file" name="Write a file" ns1:serverScript="Bug Agent: Sandbox Tool: Write File" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly \u2014 do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call \u2014 used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;},&quot;path&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Repo-relative file path.&quot;},&quot;content&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The file's full new content.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;,&quot;path&quot;,&quot;content&quot;]}">
        <documentation>Write a file's COMPLETE content into the target app's working tree, creating it if it does not exist. Overwrites the whole file — always include every line, not a diff.</documentation>
        <script>pass</script>
      </scriptTask>
      <serviceTask id="run_tests" name="Run the test suite" ns1:serviceType="connector" ns1:connectorId="agent_sandbox" ns1:operation="run_tests" ns1:connectorParams="{&quot;target_app&quot;: &quot;{{ task_data.target_app }}&quot;, &quot;git_branch&quot;: &quot;{{ task_data.git_branch }}&quot;, &quot;work_item_description&quot;: &quot;{{ task_data.work_item_description }}&quot;}" ns1:failOnError="true" ns1:aiToolParams="{&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;target_app&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The installed app to operate on, e.g. one_bpmn. Must match a real app in this bench exactly \u2014 do not guess.&quot;},&quot;git_branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The branch this work started from. Use the exact same value on every call for one work order.&quot;},&quot;work_item_description&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The work order in plain words, unchanged across every call \u2014 used to compute the same working branch each time.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;target_app&quot;,&quot;git_branch&quot;,&quot;work_item_description&quot;]}">
        <documentation>Run the target app's real test suite against the working tree as it currently stands. Use this to check your own work before you finish — open_pull_request re-runs tests itself before opening, but that only decides pass/fail, it doesn't help you fix anything.</documentation>
      </serviceTask>
    </adHocSubProcess>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="bug_programmer_00b7e913">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_1">
        <ns4:Bounds x="160" y="180" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="read_instruction_di" bpmnElement="read_instruction">
        <ns4:Bounds x="250" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_merge_di" bpmnElement="gw_merge" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="400" y="173" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="work_di" bpmnElement="work">
        <ns4:Bounds x="500" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_needs_tools_di" bpmnElement="gw_needs_tools" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="650" y="173" width="50" height="50"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="633" y="130" width="85" height="27"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="write_a2a_result_di" bpmnElement="write_a2a_result">
        <ns4:Bounds x="750" y="158" width="100" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_1_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_1">
        <ns4:Bounds x="900" y="180" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="bug_programmer_tools_di" bpmnElement="bug_programmer_tools" isExpanded="true">
        <ns4:Bounds x="-10" y="380" width="1310" height="370"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_list_files" bpmnElement="list_files">
        <ns4:Bounds x="285" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_read_file" bpmnElement="read_file">
        <ns4:Bounds x="475" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_edit_file" bpmnElement="edit_file">
        <ns4:Bounds x="855" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_write_file" bpmnElement="write_file">
        <ns4:Bounds x="1045" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="di_run_tests" bpmnElement="run_tests">
        <ns4:Bounds x="95" y="440" width="150" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_1">
        <ns5:waypoint x="196" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="250" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_2">
        <ns5:waypoint x="350" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="400" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_3">
        <ns5:waypoint x="450" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="500" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_4">
        <ns5:waypoint x="600" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="650" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_call_tools_di" bpmnElement="Flow_call_tools">
        <ns5:waypoint x="675" y="223"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="675" y="380"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="686" y="289" width="49" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_5">
        <ns5:waypoint x="700" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="750" y="198"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="717" y="180" width="15" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_tools_back_di" bpmnElement="Flow_tools_back">
        <ns5:waypoint x="425" y="380"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="425" y="223"/>
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
          <ns4:Bounds x="339" y="283" width="82" height="14"/>
        </bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_6">
        <ns5:waypoint x="850" y="198"/>
        <ns5:waypoint x="900" y="198"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</definitions>